{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791542278,"nonce":"j9s3TGfuEl0lOS8uBDPahV0L7DE=","message":"Ash milestone d516e99 removes duplicated SSA AIR/serialization ownership, makes OSR metadata lazy, frees retired SSA bodies, trims finished vector capacity, and bounds strong optimized reuse to 8 MiB plus 2 MiB per lowered-callee module cache. Global weak identity preserves live bodies during eviction. The native hdlls and Ashui sources are unchanged by this milestone; runners use the rebuilt sibling Ash release binary.\n\nSettled TreeMotion/TreeGc baseline-after allocation profiles remove 39.47 MiB of live native malloc allocations (117.79 -\u003e 78.32, excluding untouched GC reservations). Canonical AIR storage is ~16 MiB, including ~10.4 MiB IR and ~5.6 MiB serialization; strong reuse residency is ~7 MiB under its 8 MiB bound. The new SSA-root attribution is inlined differently, so compare total allocation ownership rather than claiming the walker uses zero memory.\n\nFour uninstrumented application-preset window runs show mean physical footprint 188.99 -\u003e 171.02 MiB (individual baseline 175.66/202.33; after 171.99/170.06). Idle CPU \u003c0.024%, frame-work p95 1.2-1.4ms. This is ~18 MiB mean footprint saving; native live-allocation savings do not imply the same RSS saving on every run.\n\n203 AIR tests, 3 cache tests, the SSA lifetime test, existing Ashui pixel suite, 18 baseline behavior comparisons across interpreter/Cranelift/LLVM, cast/f32/typed-read tests and OSR counter parity pass. Existing Ash issue 316cce8 remains for the macOS forced-retier routing gate; a controlled threshold exercised the actual OSR retier and preserved counters/pointer/float/phi state.\n\nArtifacts: .ashui/memory-comparison/heap-112154, heap-112239, air-pair-112522/report.json, air-behavior-112304/report.json, retier-controlled-113152. Ash f60b855 records the fix and remaining possible retirement/serialization reductions; it stays open for those follow-ups.","files":null}]}